WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.395
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:13.679 --> 00:00:15.220
MATT FEIGAL: Google
opens a new cloud

00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:16.420
region in the Netherlands.

00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:19.070
What does that mean and why
are we so proud of that?

00:00:19.070 --> 00:00:21.940
I'm Matt Feigal, and when I'm
not working on the Google Wind

00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:23.971
project to guarantee
sunny skies,

00:00:23.971 --> 00:00:25.720
my team helps companies
in the Netherlands

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:27.460
learn how to use Google Cloud.

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:29.650
Let's start with the question
of what a region means

00:00:29.650 --> 00:00:31.060
in the first place.

00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:34.510
With this opening, Google
Cloud Platform products

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:37.180
are now offered and hosted
from the Netherlands.

00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:41.180
That makes us the 14th Google
Cloud region in the world.

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:43.750
So here, on the spot where
Google's transatlantic cable

00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:46.840
enters Europe, we now have a
state-of-the-art data center

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:50.050
that houses our Google
Cloud Platform products.

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:52.120
The great thing is our
Netherlands data center

00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:54.610
is one of the largest and
most efficient data centers

00:00:54.610 --> 00:00:55.600
in the world.

00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:57.880
Everything you need
to set up your cloud

00:00:57.880 --> 00:00:59.880
and make it scalable,
you will find here--

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:04.510
from compute to big data,
storage, and networking.

00:01:04.510 --> 00:01:06.430
We are especially
proud of this location

00:01:06.430 --> 00:01:08.440
because it's all
about green energy.

00:01:08.440 --> 00:01:10.330
Together with Eneco,
we have invested

00:01:10.330 --> 00:01:13.270
in a wind farm that supplies
the energy for this data center,

00:01:13.270 --> 00:01:16.810
making it completely
CO2 neutral.

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:19.990
For our customers, this means
better performance, lower

00:01:19.990 --> 00:01:22.019
latency, and more flexibility.

00:01:22.019 --> 00:01:24.310
You can choose to allocate
your applications or storage

00:01:24.310 --> 00:01:26.620
environment in one
place or spread them

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:28.700
over multiple locations.

00:01:28.700 --> 00:01:31.420
In the Netherlands, we have
so many great local customers

00:01:31.420 --> 00:01:35.590
like bol.com, nu.nl,
MessageBird, Weeronline,

00:01:35.590 --> 00:01:38.410
Blendle, and Philips
Hue to name a few.

00:01:38.410 --> 00:01:40.390
Take Philips
Lighting for example.

00:01:40.390 --> 00:01:42.760
It's incredibly important
that the Hue platform

00:01:42.760 --> 00:01:44.840
works as quickly as possible.

00:01:44.840 --> 00:01:47.440
If you switch your light
on or off via the app,

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:50.049
it's important that your
light responds right away.

00:01:50.049 --> 00:01:52.590
Because Philip Lighting runs
the entire back end on our Cloud

00:01:52.590 --> 00:01:55.554
Platform, their users
see great performance,

00:01:55.554 --> 00:01:57.220
even if the signal
goes all the way back

00:01:57.220 --> 00:01:59.140
to your lamp via satellites.

00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:01.260
For me, the most
important reason

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:02.830
to open a region
in the Netherlands

00:02:02.830 --> 00:02:05.480
is because we are here
for the long term.

00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:07.960
Here at Google, we are serious
about the cloud business.

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:09.699
And now, we are
your new neighbor

00:02:09.699 --> 00:02:12.040
right here, right next door.

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:13.690
Consider this an invitation.

00:02:13.690 --> 00:02:15.610
Feel free to reach
out or even visit us

00:02:15.610 --> 00:02:17.562
about how we can help
you to use Google Cloud.

00:02:17.562 --> 00:02:18.270
Talk to you soon.

00:02:18.270 --> 00:02:21.620
[MUSIC PLAYING]

